  "id": "funnel_oe_physician_power",
  "reference": "Detectability and per-point intervals on a physician-scale O/E funnel. Twelve physicians, expected deaths 3.2 to 70. The point sorted first (E=3.2, 8 observed, O/E=2.50) does NOT flag despite 2.5x expected mortality: min_detectable_oe = 4.2659 says an 80%-power flag there would need a true O/E of 4.27, and the Garwood 95% CI (1.0793, 4.9260) says the truth is anywhere from barely elevated to fivefold. Meanwhile the last physician flags at only O/E=1.77 because 62 expected events buy twenty times the resolution. That inversion \u2014 a lower ratio flagging while a higher one does not \u2014 is what the funnel is for and what readers misread. Eight of twelve points cannot detect even a doubling, so summary.underpowered is true and power_note is composed. Detectability event matches signal semantics exactly (_sigma_signals flags strictly y > ucl, so O >= floor(ucl*E)+1); CIs are exact Garwood via Poisson mean inversion, independent of the center line.",
